WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.800
- For a castle straight
out of a fairytale,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.247
look no further than
the Alcázar of Segovia.

00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:10.914
(playful music)

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:19.690
Located in Central Spain, the
Alcázar of Segovia is one of

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.013
the country's most visited
and distinctive landmarks.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.180
Built in the 12th century, the Alcázar has

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.610
served many functions over the years.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.400
A fortress, a royal
palace, a state prison,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.090
an artillery college, and most recently,

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.910
a museum and military archive.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.940
However, it's most famous
function could arguably be

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.650
that it served as an inspiration

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.933
in some of the most iconic Disney films.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.200
The similarities between
Segovia and “Cinderella”

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.480
can be found in the
buildings brick facade,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.260
turrets, and location, perched high above

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.660
the neighboring countryside.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.450
Walt Disney also went
on the reproduce Segovia

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.860
as the Queen's castle in “Snow White,”

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.033
with it appearing in the film
in it's almost exact form.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.670
If you can make it up more than 150 stairs

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.110
to the top of the tower,
you will be rewarded

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.413
with stunning views fit for a queen.

